# Form: short handoff

Use to continue one bounded task. Default: the task's authorized temporary area or
tracker, not a permanent report chain. Most handoffs need only the body below; if
explicitly retained as durable knowledge, add the optional passport. Copy only the
selected payload; [metadata](../../references/metadata.md) governs durable records.
Essential: next result, base/dirty/scope, owners/constraints, checks/limits and exact
remainder. Remove irrelevant optional fields; never paste secrets or private logs.

## Optional durable passport

```yaml
---
id: "{{project_id}}-HANDOFF-{{unique_id}}"
title: "{{bounded_task}} — continuation"
kind: handoff
status: draft
created: "{{created_iso_date}}"
updated: "{{updated_iso_date}}"
areas: ["{{affected_area}}"]
summary: "{{next_result_and_current_limit}}"
---
```

## Body payload

```markdown
# Continue {{bounded_task}}

- Result / finish criterion: {{specific_next_outcome_and_stop}}.
- Base / dirty: {{exact_source_and_unrelated_changes_to_preserve}}.
- Allowed paths / exclusions: {{finite_write_scope_and_protected_areas}}.
- Sources / owners: {{actual_rule_contract_and_implementation_routes}}.
- Done / evidence: {{actual_result_commands_raw_exits_and_limits}}.
- Required next: {{one_action_or_exact_blocker_owner_and_question}}.
- Review / save authority: {{who_may_accept_write_index_commit_or_publish}}.

This snapshot does not change policy, confer new permissions, or turn a prior PASS
into proof for changed artifacts. Reuse unchanged evidence only after impact analysis.
```
